{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>YHWH</b> — The reason this is mentioned: then we remember what we were praying. He mentioned the revered Name in this third verse, on account of \"and by your name we are called,\" which is the revered and awesome Name that is eternal, as I explained in Sefer HaShem."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 80, :notes {0 "Resolved ה' in the lemma as YHWH per divine-name rules; ה' within the running text likewise rendered YHWH. The phrase ובשמך נקרא appears to be an allusion to a verse formula rather than a direct quotation marker."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:35:38.452617632Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}